WEBVTT

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.960
The next sketch must be hidden there.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.990
So this was Galileo's secret code.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.880
I want to go home...

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.090
"That summer, due to your sudden appearance...

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.550
"I learned about an emotion unique to humanity:

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.640
"that terribly ambiguous, abstract notion

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.410
"known as love, which is subject to neither proof nor verification."

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.270
What are you mumbling about?

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.230
Nothing, nothing.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.270
I was just talking to myself.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.860
Hocchii, would I be able pilot this goldfish mecha too?

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.620
It isn't a goldfish, Hazuki-chan. It's the <i>Galileo</i>!

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.950
You don't need to sound so snobby when you say it.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.410
Do you think that "Galileo"

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.460
is a bad name?

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.750
No, it's fine.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:07.960
It's rather fitting.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.680
Do you want to read the manual?

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.370
Ugh, I suck with manuals.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.620
It isn't that hard.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.100
And Grande Rosso will provide support.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.250
K-Kaa-nee...

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.930
According to the first sketch,

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:44.050
the next clue should be hidden in a ruin somewhere in this forest, but...

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.920
We're hitting a dead end already?

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.250
What now?

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.260
We can't give up yet.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:56.050
This park was only completed five years ago.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.600
We should be able to find somebody that was here around then.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.430
Doesn't that sound a bit like searching for a needle in a haystack?

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.470
Aren't we being kind of sloppy?

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.400
Fieldwork is a key aspect of archaeology!

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.310
I intend to be a prosecutor, not an archaeologist.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:12.020
I'm not going.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.780
Don't be so selfish, Kakkii.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.860
Isn't Hocchibi better at this sort of thing?

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.030
She's the smart one.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.490
That was uncalled for—

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.660
Hey, wait!

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:28.750
Oh, well.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.500
I guess it'll just be us, Hocchii.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:33.410
Hocchii?

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.500
O-Okay.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.260
Okay then, be sure the police don't find you.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.760
Eh? You aren't coming with us?

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.310
I handle the brainwork.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.640
Then <i>I</i> should be the one staying behind!

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.610
You're having so much run right now, aren't you?

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.740
Building some super machine like this, saving us

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.110
and just being great at everything.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.240
Kaa-nee...

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.000
Ow...

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.590
Sorry!

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.960
W-W-Wai—

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:36.610
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:36.610
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:44.410
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:44.410
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:51.660
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:51.660
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.750
shinkuromanika

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.750
Synchromanica

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.290
itsu no ma ni ka

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.290
Before I know it

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.460
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.460
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:04.760
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:04.760
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:11.270
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:11.270
I can hear someone's dream

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:18.230
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:18.230
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:31.040
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:31.040
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.370
shinkuromanika

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.370
Synchromanica

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.500
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.500
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.550
shinkuromanika

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.550
Synchromanica

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.760
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.760
The synchrony of your life

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.370
Snow gift

00:04:57.890 --> 00:04:58.810
I owe you one.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.320
When times are tough,
people ought to help each other.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.070
That's my brand of justice.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.360
Are you sure about this?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.760
You're giving some dirty, smelly stranger

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.330
the little food we have left...

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:14.290
Yeah, he's dirty and smelly, but how could we <i>not</i> help him?

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.660
I don't get it.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.040
All right, then! I'm going to call Anhedo-san.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.130
You two wait here.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:20.840
Huh?

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.210
You're leaving, Haa-nee?

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:25.090
Kakkii will keep you company. You'll be fine.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.800
Stop being such a busybody.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.550
Meddling is also my brand of justice.

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:37.520
I understand.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.200
Now, then...

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:56.000
Not to look a gift horse in the mouth, but this is some strange food.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.040
It's rather sweet.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.420
Oh, it's Japanese candy.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.830
I like it, but...

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.250
My name is Herman Hans.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.050
I like red bean pancakes more than that candy—

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.930
This is a micro doctor, isn't it?

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.340
You know about it?

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:14.850
It's a mini robot that can do all sorts of medical procedures, right?

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.060
How old are you?

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.690
You're kind of smelly...

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.850
Oh, sorry.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:25.530
Come to think of it, my daughter was always complaining about that too.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:26.920
You have a daughter?

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.610
She loved science.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.160
You probably could've become good friends with her.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.870
Just like me!

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:35.740
I'm not needed, am I?

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:38.130
Nothing!

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.170
What is your daughter doing now?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:46.660
She caught an unusual disease—one not treatable by typical surgical procedures...

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:50.430
I developed the micro doctor to save her.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.480
Huh?

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.260
But I thought the micro doctor

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.430
was never finished.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.560
The micro doctor was completed.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.800
But the surgery was performed too late.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.690
I'm so sorry.

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:09.700
It was all for nothing.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.820
I couldn't save my own daughter.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.120
My research, my life... All for nothing.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:19.200
I'm glad to hear Hans-san regained his energy.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.040
Yeah.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.040
I'm a little worried about him, though.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.200
Can you really afford to worry about others?

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.710
Stop getting involved with weirdos.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.940
It's like Kazuki-chan says...

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:33.720
Right now we have to focus on looking after ourselves.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.150
Right.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:39.680
I'll do some more research on the sketches.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:43.780
In the meantime, could you go buy supplies?

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:44.810
Sure.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.570
I've been wearing the same clothes since we left Toscana

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.700
and we have no food at all.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.340
Let's go, Hocchii!

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.240
Haa-nee, what about Kaa-nee?

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.740
We just need to give her some space for now.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.490
Oh, and try not to draw any attention to yourselves.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:03.250
You're wanted fugitives!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.670
Got it.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:13.680
Wow, it's been a while since I last visited a place like this.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.390
H-Haa-nee, you really stand out.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.640
Isn't that why we're wearing disguises?

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.400
Hey...

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:27.530
Look.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:32.570
Okay... Food, necessities, clothes...

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.650
Was there anything else we needed?

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:36.780
Haa-nee, wait here.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.040
Hocchii, you want these?

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:42.930
Yeah.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:45.790
We could definitely use them.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.880
Are you sure it was okay to buy so much?

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.090
Why not?

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:58.550
Anna-san seems to have a sponsor or something.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:03.120
Oh, let's buy something for Hans-san too.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.690
Wow, you aren't normally so outgoing.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:06.640
Yeah.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:09.440
Somehow, he reminded me of Papa.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.650
Oh, I guess they are kind of similar.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.200
Like, they both just scream homelessness.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:17.740
That's mean, Haa-nee.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.200
But you're laughing, Hocchii.

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.090
I wonder how Papa's doing.

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:28.370
I'm sure he's fine.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.340
But let's hurry and find the sketch so we can go get him.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:36.220
Yeah, remember how Papa said that we
should be the ones to solve the mystery?

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:37.890
That's right.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.050
We'll do this together with Kakkii.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:41.720
Yeah!

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:47.440
Th-The <i>Ganymede</i> guys?

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:49.900
Don't put up a fight.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.690
If you try anything funny, your sister will...

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.990
I'm sorry!

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:04.870
Sorry, did I hit you?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.870
Hocchii, you're amazing!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:08.870
Girlie!

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:10.890
You just pulled a killing machine on—

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:13.130
Let's get out of here!

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.590
W-Wait!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.300
Whoa, what a catch.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.890
Ah, crap!

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:23.850
Why you...

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:27.140
Take that, BlaGany!

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:27.980
Wait—

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:29.650
A snowman?

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.350
This way!

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:43.650
Damn them.

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:45.120
We'll take the stairs!

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:50.330
Nice, Haa-nee.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:51.500
Remember that trick.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.630
It's handy.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:57.510
What now?

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:59.760
Hocchii, jump!

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:05.220
Hurry up, Hocchii!

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:06.960
No, I can't!

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:08.390
There they are!

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.730
Get to the other side!

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.480
Come on, Hocchii!

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.110
I can't.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.150
You can!

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:15.730
Jump!

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.740
Hocchii!

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.590
Is Hocchibi okay?

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.800
I don't know.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.650
She seems to be in a lot of pain.

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:42.340
N-No...

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:46.430
Damn it, we can't take her to a doctor because we'd be discovered.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:47.640
What should we do?

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:49.140
A doctor?

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:53.480
The micro doctor...

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.230
Micro...
What are you talking about?

00:11:56.230 --> 00:12:00.740
Hocchibi said that Hans-san built some kind of mecha medic.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.410
No way! That guy made something like that?

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.620
Hazu-nee, keep watch over Hocchibi!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.240
Are you serious, Kakkii?

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:14.620
Kakkii, what's eating you?

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:20.460
I just want to go home!

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:23.550
It's either us or them.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.930
There's no easy way out!

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:32.930
I know that!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:33.690
But...

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.230
Hans-san, are you there?

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:42.710
Oh, you're that girl...

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.950
Please save Hocchibi!

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.090
What happened?

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:50.840
She was chased by air pirates and got hurt real bad!

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:52.450
Get her to a doctor, now!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:53.960
We can't go to a hospital!

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.960
There's an arrest warrant out for us

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.960
and we're being chased by dangerous people...

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:00.170
Wh-Who are you people?

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.710
From Galileo's inheritance to becoming wanted fugitives,

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.170
it's all been such crap.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.470
Everyone always sides with Hocchibi too.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.900
But still, I can't let Hocchibi die!

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:14.430
I'm stubborn and awkward, and I'm not honest with myself,

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:15.980
so I don't want to change...

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:19.980
But I know I can't stay like this.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.730
Please, Hans-san...

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:23.940
Save her with the micro doctor!

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.950
So you don't want to lose your family?

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:31.410
Hans-san, about your daughter...

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.160
After what happened,

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:36.410
I can see why you'd get fed up with everything.

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:38.730
I'm sorry for being selfish.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:42.340
But... But even so, I want you to save her!

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.840
You need my help, right?

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.050
Yeah.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:50.450
But first, step back...

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:52.930
Or you'll pick up my stench.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:02.230
First, secure a stable electrical source!

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:03.150
Okay.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.240
Anna-san, we're going to boot up the goldfish!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.580
Huh? I don't know how.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:08.820
I don't, either.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:10.660
I'm not good with manuals.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.800
Right! The manual!

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.620
Kazuki-chan, wait!

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:21.920
"Voice recognition"...

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.880
Grande Rosso, activate!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.880
Okay, activating the <i>Galileo</i>!

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.220
Nice, Kakkii!

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.640
Good, now I can charge the micro doctor.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:39.190
Just wait, Bambina.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.900
Hans-san, isn't it ready yet?

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:42.940
Don't rush me.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:45.900
Once it's charged and I run the final diagnostics,

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.590
we'll be able to start.

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:50.210
An enemy is headed our way.

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:52.950
It's the <i>Black Ganymede</i>!

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:55.660
We have to get out of here!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.580
Damn their timing!

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:00.500
I'll try to pilot this.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.670
Kakkii?

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:02.880
You think you can?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.000
I don't know!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.090
But I have to try!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.790
The <i>Galileo</i> is about to launch!

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.140
It worked.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.840
Um, next...

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:26.320
All right, it's time for you to hand over the inheritance!

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:28.100
I have to do this!

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:30.570
Okay, I'll back you up.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:37.410
Whoa!

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.920
Nice move... However!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.340
Quick thinking, Kazuki-chan.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.430
Hans-san, are you still working on the prep?

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:55.050
I just finished the final diagnostics.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.560
We just need to land in a safe location.

00:15:57.980 --> 00:15:59.800
Talk about a tall order.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:04.520
Espress Ione!

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:09.070
Watch out!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:13.170
O-Ow... Hocchii, are you okay?

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:15.570
Hey, we can't operate in these conditions!

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.780
Now I'm pissed!

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:21.500
Haa-nee!

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:24.120
Grande Rosso, open a comms channel to the <i>Ganymede</i>!

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:25.300
Roger.

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:27.880
Opening comms channel to the <i>Black Ganymede</i>.

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:30.710
Boss, we have an incoming message.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.380
Hey, you BlaGany bastard!

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.420
B-Bambina?

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:38.220
We're in the middle of saving my sister's life!

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:40.140
We're super busy, okay?!

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.890
We don't have time to deal with chickenshits

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.940
that can only attack wounded prey!

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.400
Get bent, jackasses!

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:48.360
What's she talking about?

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:52.780
Setting Hazuki-chan aside for a moment,
we're seeing a totally different side of Kazuki-chan...

00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:57.780
We have to capitalize on this chance.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:02.910
I don't really get any of this, but I'll give it a try.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:05.840
Grande Rosso, Assault Mode!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:11.090
Grande Rosso, changing to Assault Mode!

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:16.010
Wh-What?

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.470
What's going on?

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.100
What's with that goldfish?

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.100
Who do they think they are?!

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.310
Boss, what should we do?

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.190
Shoot them down with missiles!

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.080
Roger.

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.410
Damned goldfish...

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.000
Leonardo, ready the secondary particle cannon!

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.460
Roger!

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.040
Fire!

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:58.430
They've got moves.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.720
Boss, there's nothing to worry about.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:03.770
They'll run out of time, eventually.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:05.520
Huh? What do you mean?

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:10.520
Well, when we went after Bambina and the girlie,

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.440
the girlie fell from a building...

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:16.650
Just give 'em a little time,
and I'm sure they'll throw in the towel.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.030
H-Hey, Leonardo.

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:20.620
You bastards!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.040
Amazing.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:28.000
But the ride is really rocky...

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:37.740
We'll retreat for now.

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:40.640
I just can't face Bambina this way.

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:43.490
You owe me for this!

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:47.170
I'll take it next time, fair and square, Bambina!

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:01.550
All right. Now it's my turn.

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:13.450
Here we go.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:23.010
Thank you for your help, Hans-san.

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:26.780
No, I should be thanking you.

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:30.690
But I guess we didn't learn anything about the Moon sketch, after all...

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:31.810
Moon sketch?

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.410
Or maybe it was right under our noses all along!

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:35.580
No way.

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:44.870
Yeah, it's real!

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.100
Huh? What's that?

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:50.150
Oh, I sometimes had it around while I was eating,

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:51.790
so those might be food stains.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.380
Wh-What sacrilege!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.250
So how did you come to have this, Hans-san?

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:59.510
F-Food s-stains?

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.510
After I'd quit as an engineer,

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:03.510
I was living in the forest nearby until all the trees were cut down.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.170
I found it in a broken fish statue.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:12.520
It was just the right size,
so I've been using it as a place mat.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.810
The world's cultural heritage...

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:18.440
A rare, important, precious sketch...

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:20.030
was used as a place mat...

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.200
Are you sure?

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:28.060
Yeah, you guys took good care of me.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:29.200
Consider it a parting gift.

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:31.700
Thank you!

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:35.710
I think I recovered some of my old self, too.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:40.300
God, I can't believe he doesn't understand how valuable that sketch is.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.710
Where's Hocchibi?

00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:43.840
She isn't up here.

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:46.150
Okay, never mind.

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:48.260
What?

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:51.100
Oh, I was just surprised.

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.100
Kakkii, you don't come here very often.

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:58.720
Who cares where I go on the <i>Galile</i>—
I mean, on the goldfish?

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:01.530
Kakkii...

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.610
Did she just say the <i>Galileo</i>?

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:20.520
You're so awkward, Kaa-nee.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
